   =InfoForTranslators: An option to toggle whether selected characters will act autonomously. By "selected parafolks", we mean the specific character of the family that the player has currently clicked to control. By autonomy, I mean the fact that characters can decide to do interactions on their own like eating a snack if they are hungry. If turned off, selected characters won't do anything autonomously.
   =LocalizationState:8
  i2948
   =GUID:7205318598245517760
   =Key:Settings_GameplayOptions_EnableAutonomyForOtherCharacters
   =Value:Enable Autonomy for Non-Selected Parafolks
   =OriginalValue:Enable Autonomy for Other Characters
   =InfoForTranslators:An option to toggle whether non-selected household characters will act autonomously. By "selected parafolks", I mean the specific character of the family that the player has currently clicked to control so "non-selected parafolks" means the characters of your own family that you have not currently clicked on to control (player needs to click on specific characters first to select them and give them orders). By autonomy, I mean the fact that characters can decide to do interactions on their own like eating a snack if they are hungry. If turned off, non-selected characters won't do anything autonomously.
   =LocalizationState:8
  i2949
   =GUID:7784448048297220717
